WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:02.740
Why am I going to be an idol?

00:00:02.740 --> 00:00:05.430
We call it the Zombie 
Land Saga Project, baby!

00:00:05.430 --> 00:00:07.310
Revitalizing a prefecture as local idols?

00:00:06.860 --> 00:00:09.360
That's our name now that we've been reborn!

00:00:08.930 --> 00:00:10.070
Oh, what do I do now?!

00:00:09.620 --> 00:00:11.610
It's fine. I'll back you up.

00:00:11.610 --> 00:00:13.410
Doesn't matter if you don't, 
as long as I do have what it takes!

00:00:12.230 --> 00:00:15.160
We would rather go on 
stage and fail with you.

00:00:13.750 --> 00:00:16.310
Is it okay if we... as Franchouchou...

00:00:16.310 --> 00:00:18.880
It was a crazy scheme in the first place...

00:00:18.880 --> 00:00:21.860
There's a hard deadline on this project!

00:00:21.860 --> 00:00:23.590
There's no doubt about it...

00:00:23.950 --> 00:00:25.530
They're all dead.

00:00:25.100 --> 00:00:28.370
Only other explanation is that they 
were revived, like a bunch of zombies.

00:00:32.020 --> 00:00:34.320
Even if we have nothing else, 
we still have the future.

00:00:34.320 --> 00:00:37.220
A lowest point? Starting over from 
zero? That's just part of the saga.

00:00:37.550 --> 00:00:39.970
Even if we burn out in the 
process, we'll make it come true!

00:00:39.970 --> 00:00:41.890
This is where our revenge begins!

00:00:42.390 --> 00:00:47.400
<b>Zombie Land Saga 
Revenge</b>

00:00:47.560 --> 00:00:52.690
<b>The SAGA of How These Zombies
 Will Get Their Revenge</b>

00:02:00.010 --> 00:02:02.810
<b>Three Weeks After the Arpino Concert</b>

00:02:00.010 --> 00:02:02.810
<b>January 17th, 2019</b>

00:02:03.370 --> 00:02:06.940
Damn, the article makes us look awesome!

00:02:07.210 --> 00:02:11.270
I suppose it really isn't Franchouchou 
without all seven of us.

00:02:12.800 --> 00:02:15.320
It talks about how our first album
 went on sale after the concert,

00:02:15.320 --> 00:02:19.140
and it became a one-of-a-kind 
smash hit in the Saga idol scene!

00:02:19.140 --> 00:02:21.780
It wouldn't have killed them to 
call it a "magical hit," though!

00:02:21.780 --> 00:02:24.030
<b>Article by
 Arata Ookoba</b>

00:02:22.010 --> 00:02:24.020
It's that writer who always covers us.

00:02:24.530 --> 00:02:28.210
He has given criticism sometimes, 
so we can trust his opinion.

00:02:28.620 --> 00:02:30.160
We should pay attention to what he says.

00:02:30.880 --> 00:02:33.490
Hell, I bet we can rope in a 
crowd of a thousand next time!

00:02:33.670 --> 00:02:36.680
Come on, getting cocky like that is exactly 
how we'll end up making a mistake.

00:02:36.680 --> 00:02:38.060
We don't want to be overconfident.

00:02:38.060 --> 00:02:39.590
Let's stay sharp and keep working steadily.

00:02:39.820 --> 00:02:43.500
All right, let's stay sharp 
so we don't screw up,

00:02:43.500 --> 00:02:45.050
and get that crowd of a thousand!

00:02:45.260 --> 00:02:47.220
Yeah!

00:02:47.560 --> 00:02:49.310
<b>January 18th, 2019</b>

00:02:48.210 --> 00:02:54.650
Exactly how long are you gonna be high off 
that Arpino show, you giddy zombies?!

00:02:54.880 --> 00:02:58.180
Zombies don't have the free time 
or the brains to sit on their laurels!

00:02:58.180 --> 00:02:59.900
And boom!

00:02:59.530 --> 00:03:01.070
<b>Concert</b>

00:02:59.900 --> 00:03:05.910
We're barreling right into a show at the 
Ekimae Fudosan Stadium... EFS for short!

00:03:06.510 --> 00:03:09.540
Ekimae Fudosan...?

00:03:09.990 --> 00:03:10.800
Ai-chan?

00:03:10.800 --> 00:03:13.800
I've never heard of that stadium before.

00:03:14.060 --> 00:03:16.550
Doesn't matter how fancy the name is.

00:03:16.550 --> 00:03:19.590
We're set to bring in a 
crowd of a thousand next time!

00:03:19.780 --> 00:03:23.840
It's not actually going to be 
called that until February...

00:03:24.080 --> 00:03:26.110
Someone's done their homework.

00:03:26.430 --> 00:03:28.620
The name is changing?

00:03:28.620 --> 00:03:30.350
What's it called now, though?

00:03:31.280 --> 00:03:33.570
The Best Amenity Stadium...

00:03:34.310 --> 00:03:35.740
The one in Tosu.

00:03:39.720 --> 00:03:40.760
Ai-chan...

00:03:40.760 --> 00:03:42.490
I appreciate it, but I'm okay.

00:03:43.110 --> 00:03:45.490
The real issue here is the size.

00:03:46.290 --> 00:03:49.160
I'm pretty sure its seating capacity is...

00:03:49.490 --> 00:03:50.900
Approximately 25,000.

00:03:52.360 --> 00:03:53.750
Twenty-five thousand...?

00:03:53.950 --> 00:03:55.760
That's <i>{italicize for emphasis}fifty</i> times the size of Arpino.

00:03:55.760 --> 00:03:58.290
With standing room on the 
field for even more.

00:03:58.600 --> 00:04:02.540
I'm having trouble picturing this... 
Is that a number I could beat in a fight?

00:04:02.540 --> 00:04:03.830
That's really impressive—

00:04:03.830 --> 00:04:05.050
There's no way we can pull that off!

00:04:06.960 --> 00:04:08.980
The show is scheduled for March 8th.

00:04:09.240 --> 00:04:10.390
Don't be ridiculous!

00:04:10.390 --> 00:04:13.130
This isn't Fukuoka! We're in Saga!

00:04:13.130 --> 00:04:16.490
A stadium in Saga... Iron Frill was 
able to manage it back then, but—

00:04:15.870 --> 00:04:19.560
Except y'all are a lot better now!

00:04:20.840 --> 00:04:21.820
Or what?

00:04:22.170 --> 00:04:27.620
Are you going to say that Franchouchou isn't 
as good now as Iron Frill was ten years ago?

00:04:28.560 --> 00:04:31.620
Each and every one of you is a legend...

00:04:35.650 --> 00:04:37.590
With one exception, you're all legendary.

00:04:37.590 --> 00:04:39.450
Pretty sure he was looking 
right at me just now.

00:04:39.690 --> 00:04:42.160
I chose and resurrected 
you all to save Saga!

00:04:42.160 --> 00:04:45.070
You can accomplish anything!

00:04:45.070 --> 00:04:48.730
EFS will be filled to capacity 
with Franchouchou fans!

00:04:48.970 --> 00:04:51.280
And then, once you've got the crowd on fire,

00:04:51.280 --> 00:04:54.190
you'll blow them up with the new 
song as an encore, like boom!

00:04:56.460 --> 00:05:01.570
Franchouchou's legend is going to 
keep blowing up like a cluster bomb!

00:05:03.430 --> 00:05:08.670
Look, even I can tell that Shades is 
being a bigger dumbass than ever before.

00:05:08.670 --> 00:05:10.230
Can we seriously pull this off?

00:05:10.230 --> 00:05:12.630
Normally? I'd say it's 100% impossible.

00:05:12.630 --> 00:05:14.780
It's just too unrealistic...

00:05:14.780 --> 00:05:15.980
But y'know...

00:05:15.980 --> 00:05:19.350
I know it's a little too late for us to 
start thinking about what's normal or realistic.

00:05:19.350 --> 00:05:20.510
Sure is.

00:05:20.510 --> 00:05:23.580
If Kotaro-san is serious about this...

00:05:23.580 --> 00:05:26.360
Maybe he has some kind of reason behind it?

00:05:26.360 --> 00:05:29.070
You think Tatsumi actually has a plan?

00:05:31.830 --> 00:05:34.890
Let's... try it.

00:05:35.610 --> 00:05:38.130
Do you realize what taking this on means?

00:05:38.130 --> 00:05:40.080
I dunno if we can manage it, but...

00:05:40.080 --> 00:05:44.660
If there's a place where we can all sing 
and dance together, I'm willing to try it.

00:05:44.860 --> 00:05:47.740
I want to go on stage with you 
all as many times as I can!

00:05:48.970 --> 00:05:50.250
You're on.

00:05:50.250 --> 00:05:52.850
There was a lot of trouble at Arpino, too,

00:05:52.850 --> 00:05:54.070
and we managed to get through that!

00:05:54.290 --> 00:05:57.280
If you think about it, there's never been a time 
when we weren't doing something crazy.

00:05:57.280 --> 00:05:59.790
Hell, we're already zombies.

00:05:59.790 --> 00:06:02.130
And that means there's no 
sense in chickening out.

00:06:02.330 --> 00:06:04.450
I'm honestly a little shaken at how

00:06:04.450 --> 00:06:08.340
listening to you all makes
 me believe we can accomplish this...

00:06:11.270 --> 00:06:13.310
I'm surrounded by a bunch 
of crazy optimists.

00:06:13.980 --> 00:06:17.550
If we're going to do this, we need our 
performance to be even better than Arpino.

00:06:17.770 --> 00:06:21.170
Anything less than our full effort 
is bound to be a failure.

00:06:21.170 --> 00:06:23.270
Ai-chan, I hope you really 
put us through our paces!

00:06:23.470 --> 00:06:24.750
Obviously I will.

00:06:24.750 --> 00:06:27.520
This is where we address everything 
I've been letting you guys slide on so far...

00:06:27.520 --> 00:06:27.980
Yeah!

00:06:27.980 --> 00:06:29.580
That goes double for you, Sakura.

00:06:29.980 --> 00:06:31.870
But could you still be gentle, please...?

00:06:31.870 --> 00:06:33.710
Don't get soft now!

00:06:42.830 --> 00:06:45.060
Something still bugging you?

00:06:45.060 --> 00:06:47.300
Of course there is.

00:06:47.300 --> 00:06:49.670
Despite how it turned out, 
I did technically die there.

00:06:49.670 --> 00:06:52.390
Don't sweat it. It's not 
like you can die twice.

00:06:52.390 --> 00:06:55.940
I'm not sure you'd understand, considering
 you jumped off the same cliff twice.

00:06:59.520 --> 00:07:02.610
You remember what you said back at the park?

00:07:02.990 --> 00:07:07.770
I don't care if I'm a zombie. 
I will get up on stage again, and then...

00:07:09.120 --> 00:07:10.650
Let's make it happen.

00:07:10.650 --> 00:07:12.940
If anything happens, I'll clean it up.

00:07:13.180 --> 00:07:16.830
I might be the boss now, but at heart, 
I'm still the gal who leads the attack.

00:07:16.830 --> 00:07:19.200
In idol group terms, you're the leader, okay?

00:07:20.690 --> 00:07:22.130
Okay, that's scary!

00:07:22.130 --> 00:07:24.790
I didn't see either of you, 
so I thought I'd check...

00:07:24.790 --> 00:07:27.520
I-It's nothing special, I just...

00:07:27.520 --> 00:07:28.470
It'll be all right.

00:07:28.870 --> 00:07:30.900
I'll be there to back you up, too.

00:07:31.270 --> 00:07:34.100
I feel bad about eavesdropping, but...

00:07:34.290 --> 00:07:37.520
Hell yeah! Why don't we have 
a rally to get set for the show?!

00:07:37.520 --> 00:07:39.700
Seriously, we're not bikers!

00:07:42.390 --> 00:07:44.800
Yeah, yeah! Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:07:46.190 --> 00:07:49.640
Yeah, yeah. Yeah, yeah, yeah...

00:07:49.640 --> 00:07:51.110
No, that's not it.

00:07:52.630 --> 00:07:54.110
There's no way we can pull that off!

00:07:57.690 --> 00:08:00.710
Yeah, yeah, woo— No, not right.

00:08:00.700 --> 00:08:03.170
<b>March 7th, 2019</b>

00:08:00.700 --> 00:08:03.170
<b>The day before 
the show</b>

00:08:04.710 --> 00:08:06.010
Damn, that's huge.

00:08:07.330 --> 00:08:08.320
Excuse me...

00:08:08.960 --> 00:08:14.760
I was too anxious to ask before, but... 
how many tickets were presold?

00:08:14.760 --> 00:08:16.420
I didn't have any made.

00:08:17.070 --> 00:08:18.550
What are you...?!

00:08:18.550 --> 00:08:20.300
We're only selling tickets
on the day of the show.

00:08:20.660 --> 00:08:22.070
Why would you do that?!

00:08:22.270 --> 00:08:23.570
With this concert,

00:08:23.570 --> 00:08:27.210
we need to make it clear to the entire 
world that Franchouchou has risen in Saga.

00:08:27.210 --> 00:08:30.840
Which means it needs to be legendary, 
in as many aspects as possible.

00:08:30.840 --> 00:08:32.520
Ordinary methods won't cut it.

00:08:33.730 --> 00:08:36.600
Remember everything you've 
accomplished so far...

00:08:37.530 --> 00:08:38.900
Believe in Franchouchou,

00:08:39.150 --> 00:08:40.910
and believe in me!

00:08:42.870 --> 00:08:45.330
<b>March 8th, 2019</b>

00:08:42.870 --> 00:08:45.330
<b>The day of 
the show</b>

00:08:50.600 --> 00:08:54.710
The entire crowd... fits 
inside the penalty area.

00:08:55.620 --> 00:09:00.500
Uh, hey there, thanks for 
coming... today....

00:09:00.500 --> 00:09:02.580
We're... Franchouchou.

00:09:33.320 --> 00:09:35.320
Should we still call for an encore?

00:09:35.320 --> 00:09:38.050
That'd just be too cruel.

00:09:38.830 --> 00:09:40.940
Is this hell?

00:10:09.530 --> 00:10:12.530
I'm hooome!

00:10:13.580 --> 00:10:17.250
Hey, look, it's Franzhouzhou... 
Franslshslsh...

00:10:17.250 --> 00:10:20.920
Kotaro-san, you never came back. 
We were worried about you—

00:10:19.280 --> 00:10:21.230
Yeah, yeah, yeah...

00:10:21.230 --> 00:10:24.640
Kotaro-san, reporting for duty!

00:10:27.560 --> 00:10:29.520
Were you out drinking all night?

00:10:29.520 --> 00:10:36.580
Yes, I was! Cuz we're 20 
million in debt, y'know!

00:10:36.580 --> 00:10:40.910
S'pretty wild, right? Twenty million! In debt!

00:10:41.150 --> 00:10:44.120
We're in debt? For 20 million yen?!

00:10:44.120 --> 00:10:45.270
For real?

00:10:45.270 --> 00:10:46.540
I think so.

00:10:47.000 --> 00:10:51.840
It's only natural, considering the scope 
of the concert and how badly it failed.

00:10:52.430 --> 00:10:54.960
What's with all the serious faces?!

00:10:54.960 --> 00:10:57.970
Franchouchou is done! Saga's done, too!

00:10:57.970 --> 00:10:59.930
It's all over!

00:11:00.260 --> 00:11:01.680
Game over!

00:11:01.680 --> 00:11:04.140
<b>March 23rd, 2019</b>

00:11:02.480 --> 00:11:06.520
Shades has been drunk off 
his ass for two weeks now.

00:11:06.520 --> 00:11:09.870
It's been seven days since 
we ran out of food, too.

00:11:09.870 --> 00:11:13.550
W-We don't need to eat, 
though! Since we're zombies!

00:11:13.550 --> 00:11:18.030
Kotaro-san might be coming up 
with a new plan right now!

00:11:18.030 --> 00:11:19.220
I mean, he's done it before—

00:11:19.220 --> 00:11:21.060
That ass never had a plan 
in the first place!

00:11:21.060 --> 00:11:23.450
That's how this crap even happened!

00:11:23.450 --> 00:11:25.520
Don't take it out on Sakura!

00:11:25.520 --> 00:11:27.980
You're not the only one who's irritated.

00:11:27.980 --> 00:11:29.750
What should I do, then?!

00:11:29.750 --> 00:11:32.030
C-Come on, you two! Don't fight!

00:11:32.030 --> 00:11:34.630
It's times like this when we 
really need to work together!

00:11:34.630 --> 00:11:36.490
We'll figure something out!

00:11:36.490 --> 00:11:38.430
You say we should work together,

00:11:38.430 --> 00:11:42.980
but without any help, we can't do 
our makeup or even go shopping.

00:11:42.980 --> 00:11:47.670
And this entire time, that debt 
is only going to grow larger...

00:11:47.670 --> 00:11:51.050
This situation is going to need 
something more than positivity!

00:11:57.190 --> 00:11:58.410
Tae-chan?

00:11:58.660 --> 00:12:01.210
Girl... what happened to your face?

00:12:02.490 --> 00:12:03.990
<b>{Tin sign}100,000 yen
 Bank</b>

00:12:02.490 --> 00:12:03.990
<i>Don't touch! 
This belongs to Kotaro</i>

00:12:15.870 --> 00:12:17.240
She got it on her own?!

00:12:17.500 --> 00:12:18.800
Yeah, I think so.

00:12:18.800 --> 00:12:20.510
After finding Tatsumi's money?

00:12:20.510 --> 00:12:22.210
And doing her own cosmetics?

00:12:23.040 --> 00:12:24.360
That's crazy...

00:12:27.860 --> 00:12:30.670
We were wrong all along.

00:12:31.140 --> 00:12:34.420
We can do it if we try, just like Tae-chan!

00:12:35.090 --> 00:12:37.780
But we weren't even trying!

00:12:37.780 --> 00:12:40.770
"As zombies, we can't do anything 
without Tatsumi-san."

00:12:40.770 --> 00:12:43.350
We just assumed that was true and gave up.

00:12:43.600 --> 00:12:47.970
Yeah. At some point we started to 
take Kotaro-san's help for granted.

00:12:47.970 --> 00:12:50.930
You're right. That's kind of what 
happened at the EFS show, too.

00:12:50.930 --> 00:12:55.410
We assumed he'd figure something out 
as long as we tried our hardest.

00:12:55.840 --> 00:12:57.420
And that was wrong!

00:12:59.380 --> 00:13:02.500
I guess if we've got the makeup, 
we might as well use it.

00:13:02.500 --> 00:13:05.030
How are we gonna pay back the debt, then?

00:13:05.030 --> 00:13:06.020
Let's get jobs!

00:13:06.020 --> 00:13:10.770
If we can't do idol stuff right now, let's 
think of ways to make money until we can!

00:13:10.770 --> 00:13:12.520
Will I be able to help, too?

00:13:12.520 --> 00:13:13.360
Of course.

00:13:13.360 --> 00:13:14.550
We should do it.

00:13:14.550 --> 00:13:16.550
We always pull it off when 
we're cornered, anyway.

00:13:16.550 --> 00:13:18.980
From now on, we'll do 
the thinking ourselves.

00:13:18.980 --> 00:13:21.970
We won't let what's happened
 before limit us! We'll move forward!

00:13:26.360 --> 00:13:29.710
<i>That's right... In the end, I still haven't...</i>

00:13:31.020 --> 00:13:32.190
Ai-chan?

00:13:32.700 --> 00:13:33.680
Let's do it!

00:13:34.330 --> 00:13:36.920
If we can't, we're just regular zombies.

00:13:37.170 --> 00:13:41.420
Yeah! We'll figure this out 
and get our revenge!

00:13:42.050 --> 00:13:47.050
<b>Zombie Land Saga Revenge</b>

00:13:42.050 --> 00:13:47.050
<b>The Culture Grill</b>

00:13:42.050 --> 00:13:47.050
<b>Oxford (Ushizu)</b>

00:13:47.050 --> 00:13:52.060
<b>Zombie Land Saga Revenge</b>

00:13:52.060 --> 00:13:54.520
<b>February 16th, 2020</b>

00:13:55.830 --> 00:13:58.420
Well, he sure is dead.

00:13:58.420 --> 00:14:00.950
What's the rest? Is it all squid?

00:14:00.950 --> 00:14:03.010
Never seen anything like it...

00:14:03.330 --> 00:14:04.250
He's alive?!

00:14:04.610 --> 00:14:06.310
Mister, are you okay?

00:14:09.980 --> 00:14:13.080
No problems here. Just got a 
little swept away by the tide.

00:14:18.240 --> 00:14:19.790
And apparently that's what happened!

00:14:19.790 --> 00:14:21.750
Is that wild or what?!

00:14:22.070 --> 00:14:24.210
The squid man! Let's check it out!

00:14:24.210 --> 00:14:26.090
I'll let you handle it.

00:14:26.090 --> 00:14:29.510
Seriously? Is this story of yours 
that big a deal, Ookoba-san?

00:14:29.850 --> 00:14:32.640
I bet even the Tokyo pubs are 
gonna want a piece of it...

00:14:33.580 --> 00:14:34.690
Inubashiri!

00:14:34.690 --> 00:14:35.840
Oh, right!

00:14:35.840 --> 00:14:39.640
Well, I'll look forward to it while 
I'm on the trail of the Squid Man!

00:14:46.660 --> 00:14:47.600
G'morning.

00:14:47.840 --> 00:14:49.320
What happened to you?

00:14:49.320 --> 00:14:50.070
Not important.

00:14:54.510 --> 00:14:56.060
C'mon, say some—

00:14:55.230 --> 00:14:58.470
One year ago... I made a mistake.

00:14:59.290 --> 00:15:01.150
March 8th of last year...

00:15:01.150 --> 00:15:04.460
Insisting on the EFS show was a 
complete failure on my behalf.

00:15:04.750 --> 00:15:05.670
I'm sorry.

00:15:08.700 --> 00:15:10.180
And in order to make up for that...

00:15:10.470 --> 00:15:14.170
Next month, on March 8th, you'll be 
performing your revenge concert at EFS.

00:15:18.110 --> 00:15:19.950
You'll be performing your 
revenge concert at EFS.

00:15:19.950 --> 00:15:20.710
Hold—

00:15:20.710 --> 00:15:21.440
That said!

00:15:21.630 --> 00:15:25.980
This time, I'm not booking it based purely 
on momentum and self-satisfaction.

00:15:26.800 --> 00:15:30.160
Franchouchou has done a fantastic 
job of reviving in the past year.

00:15:30.960 --> 00:15:33.110
Your album and merchandise sales

00:15:33.110 --> 00:15:36.750
have been growing like the rice in the 
fields of Hamanoura and Warabino.

00:15:37.090 --> 00:15:40.360
And, more importantly,
 you have all grown a lot.

00:15:41.290 --> 00:15:44.370
Even then, EFS will 
prove to be a challenge.

00:15:44.640 --> 00:15:49.250
I'm working on a variety of advertising 
projects that will lead into the EFS show.

00:15:49.600 --> 00:15:52.880
I'm going to put everything I have 
into doing everything I possibly can.

00:15:52.880 --> 00:15:56.680
And, to make Franchouchou 
into an even bigger legend,

00:15:56.680 --> 00:15:59.140
we'll incorporate that past 
failure into our success story.

00:16:00.320 --> 00:16:02.100
That's why you want to do it on March 8th...

00:16:02.740 --> 00:16:03.260
Listen to me!

00:16:03.910 --> 00:16:06.830
The battle we're about to 
embark on will be remembered

00:16:06.830 --> 00:16:10.370
in the history of Saga as one of the 
most notable things to ever happen!

00:16:10.640 --> 00:16:14.340
Even if Saga itself is 
forced to suffer a cruel fate

00:16:14.340 --> 00:16:16.950
where it's swallowed into 
the darkness of despair,

00:16:16.950 --> 00:16:21.550
the seven of you will remain a 
shining light amidst that darkness!

00:16:22.300 --> 00:16:28.120
I chose and resurrected 
you zombies to save Saga!

00:16:28.460 --> 00:16:31.020
When you complete your revenge,

00:16:31.020 --> 00:16:36.700
it will signal the beginning 
of Saga's counterattack!

00:16:39.080 --> 00:16:40.020
Achoo.

00:16:40.280 --> 00:16:41.730
What's with the sneeze?!

00:16:41.730 --> 00:16:42.660
It's not a problem.

00:16:42.660 --> 00:16:43.720
I thought it was cute.

00:16:43.720 --> 00:16:45.520
You killed the moment, dude...

00:16:44.930 --> 00:16:46.790
P-P-Pipe down!

00:16:47.940 --> 00:16:50.400
<b>February 17th, 2020</b>

00:16:54.250 --> 00:16:56.820
Kotaro Tatsumi-san, right?

00:16:58.300 --> 00:17:01.630
The name's Arata Ookoba. I'm part 
of <i>Sagazine</i>'s editorial staff.

00:17:02.550 --> 00:17:05.340
I always read your articles.

00:17:05.630 --> 00:17:08.130
That show last year was quite a shame...

00:17:08.130 --> 00:17:12.270
But lately it seems your girls have 
really been outdoing themselves.

00:17:13.510 --> 00:17:16.270
I assume you're here to keep 
past mistakes in mind?

00:17:16.270 --> 00:17:18.370
Group policy is that I don't do personal—

00:17:18.370 --> 00:17:23.180
You do this job for long enough and you 
make all kinds of acquaintances all over.

00:17:23.180 --> 00:17:26.470
That said, it took me a while 
to connect the dots this time.

00:17:27.660 --> 00:17:30.570
Sakura Minamoto-san... Saki Nikaido-san...

00:17:30.910 --> 00:17:33.560
Ai Mizuno-san... Junko Konno-san...

00:17:33.560 --> 00:17:36.010
Lily Hoshikawa aka Masao Go-san...

00:17:36.010 --> 00:17:37.160
And Tae Yamada-san.

00:17:37.610 --> 00:17:40.040
They've all passed away.

00:17:40.870 --> 00:17:44.510
Sadly, I wasn't able to dig 
anything up on Number Five.

00:17:46.450 --> 00:17:47.880
You have to tell me...

00:17:48.780 --> 00:17:50.700
Just what are these girls?

00:17:51.470 --> 00:17:54.060
I have pictures like this, too.

00:17:54.960 --> 00:17:57.780
I can have the graves dug up, you know.

00:17:58.630 --> 00:18:00.670
Why would you write about this?

00:18:00.670 --> 00:18:07.670
To put a stop to you trying to profit off 
these dead girls by making them into idols...

00:18:07.670 --> 00:18:09.580
Would you accept that as a reason?

00:18:11.190 --> 00:18:16.130
You can keep quiet, but once the article 
gets published, the truth will be out there.

00:18:16.440 --> 00:18:20.070
I've gotta wonder what 
the public will think...

00:18:21.600 --> 00:18:24.910
Franchouchou will be performing 
a concert here next month.

00:18:25.880 --> 00:18:27.150
A revenge concert.

00:18:27.150 --> 00:18:28.600
Are you insane?

00:18:28.600 --> 00:18:31.330
What would be the point of 
re-enacting that disaster?

00:18:31.330 --> 00:18:33.660
You need to stop turning the 
dead into entertainment!

00:18:34.690 --> 00:18:38.800
No matter what article you write, 
there's no stopping Franchouchou.

00:18:41.900 --> 00:18:44.490
I'm not letting this revenge show happen!

00:18:55.360 --> 00:18:56.890
You okay down there?

00:19:01.370 --> 00:19:06.090
Sounds like this isn't going to work out 
like it did with the high school girl.

00:19:06.090 --> 00:19:10.630
Though, I'm kind of surprised 
no one caught on sooner.

00:19:10.630 --> 00:19:13.300
There's more in your way than 
just this reporter, too.

00:19:13.830 --> 00:19:16.540
You might be lucky if all 
that happens next time

00:19:16.540 --> 00:19:18.940
is a few scratches and your 
clothes getting stolen...

00:19:18.940 --> 00:19:23.460
I don't care what gets in the way. 
I'm going to make this EFS show a success.

00:19:23.460 --> 00:19:25.340
I'm not making the same mistake again.

00:19:26.170 --> 00:19:32.550
To think that the gloomy, half-crazed kid I 
met 12 years ago could pull all this off...

00:19:32.550 --> 00:19:37.230
Do you think anyone who wasn't gloomy and 
half-crazed would ever have believed you?

00:19:37.420 --> 00:19:40.340
That you're fighting a curse that's been at 
work in this land for thousands of years...

00:19:40.340 --> 00:19:41.650
That you're immortal....

00:19:42.280 --> 00:19:44.710
And that you can revive the dead?

00:19:45.020 --> 00:19:47.490
You got what you wanted, though.

00:19:47.490 --> 00:19:48.710
Not yet.

00:19:49.700 --> 00:19:52.950
I still have to prevent your prophecy.

00:19:54.150 --> 00:19:58.440
With the beginning of the Reiwa era, 
Saga will face a cataclysmic threat...

00:19:58.440 --> 00:20:02.050
A cataclysm wherein no one 
will think of Saga anymore,

00:20:02.050 --> 00:20:05.690
and it will even vanish from their memories.

00:20:06.050 --> 00:20:09.460
Things are already looking bad enough 
with the shrinking population...

00:20:09.750 --> 00:20:15.090
In that case, I just need to create something
 people will never forget, here in Saga.

00:20:15.310 --> 00:20:20.590
Taking girls who were killed by the curse, 
who would have brought glory to Saga...

00:20:20.590 --> 00:20:24.160
Gathering them together 
and making them into an idol group.

00:20:24.160 --> 00:20:25.870
I'll admit it's a hell of an idea.

00:20:25.870 --> 00:20:28.940
This Mount Mifuneyama Rakuen 
Project of yours...

00:20:28.940 --> 00:20:31.150
It's the Zombie Land Saga Project.

00:20:31.150 --> 00:20:32.340
Right, that.

00:20:33.500 --> 00:20:36.710
The world of man will always be 
shaped by the actions of men...

00:20:37.820 --> 00:20:39.040
You're wrong there.

00:20:39.990 --> 00:20:43.640
It will be shaped by men and zombies.

00:20:47.670 --> 00:20:52.640
<i>Overnight and into tomorrow morning, 
there's a severe rain warning for Kyushu.</i>

00:20:54.610 --> 00:20:58.620
<i>Coastal areas and rivers 
are under a flood warning...</i>

00:20:54.800 --> 00:20:56.620
That's a lot of rain...

00:20:56.620 --> 00:20:58.720
I wonder if Kotaro-san's okay.

00:20:58.720 --> 00:21:00.080
He'll be fine.

00:21:00.080 --> 00:21:01.450
I hope so...

00:21:01.450 --> 00:21:04.250
Maybe we can hit him up with the 
waterproof spray this time!

00:21:04.890 --> 00:21:08.130
Our final revenge is 
getting started tomorrow.

00:21:08.130 --> 00:21:09.240
Make sure to get lots of rest.

00:21:09.570 --> 00:21:10.320
Yeah.

00:21:16.710 --> 00:21:18.400
There we go.

00:21:18.400 --> 00:21:20.880
I have to admit, this is a 
hell of a thing to write...

00:21:22.280 --> 00:21:25.230
They'll be performing a concert 
here at EFS next month.

00:21:26.500 --> 00:21:28.880
Can't believe he'd put the 
dead on display like that.

00:21:28.350 --> 00:21:30.100
